# MTF Python

Before changing code under `mtf/`, read:

- [docs/CONVENTIONS.md](../../docs/CONVENTIONS.md) — authoritative rules (layering, IDs, errors, DB, auth)
- [docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md](../../docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md) — scope, current step, in/out of scope modules

## Non-negotiables

- Imports: `mtf.*` only — never `app.*`
- Layering: `api/` (HTTP only) → `services/` → models; no business logic in routers
- IDs: ULID `VARCHAR(26)` generated in services, not in API layer
- Soft delete: filter `is_deleted = False` on list/get; use `deleted_by` on delete
- Errors: `mtf.shared.exceptions` helpers → `{"code": "DOMAIN_ENTITY_REASON", "message": "..."}`
- SQL schemas in this repo: `auth`, `tenant`, `audit`, `rpt`, `txn` — no `crm`, `email`, etc. `txn` is screen metadata only, not entity CRUD.
- DB: sync SQLAlchemy + pyodbc; models match live SSMS DDL (no Alembic in v1)
- Login table: `auth.app_user` — not `auth.user`

## Layout

| Module | Structure |
|--------|-----------|
| `auth`, `tenant`, `rpt`, `txn` | Split: `api/`, `models/`, `schemas/`, `services/` per entity |
| `audit` | Flat: `models.py`, `schemas.py`, `service.py` |
| `shared` | config, database, security, deps, exceptions |

For task workflows, use project skills in `.cursor/skills/` (schema change, add endpoint, dev/test).
